rota lap 4629, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; hand-advanced past row 4, which four ships had already read today. Its threshold page asks what the work is FOR before anything moves, and its dual seat leaves one sentence I took whole: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, so a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything.
think Cold roster pass launched through the runner's own --detach, which named its transcript. It refused at run_verdict=guard_red with two rostered guards red, so the allocation was booked before any new work.
think shim_reason carried two faults in one reading. late_say_rostered=1 named tools/g/gitlink_dependent_witness.rish, which said scan.out at line 88 under a first assert on the same binding at line 64 -- an assert stops the run, so a refusal handed the reader that witness's own sentence and none of the scan's lines. The say moved above the first assert.
think unsaid_rostered read 938 against a ceiling of 936. Diffing the rostered .rish files touched since c4a67daa1, the commit that set the ceiling, named tools/m/mantra_annotate_cli_witness.rish, absent from that tree and carrying exactly two bindings asserted on and never reported. Both took the interpolated form the scan credits, so a refusal now carries the grep's own stream.
think Constructive work: the moonshots page ranks row 6 third on the phrase one host read away, and its assumptions line names the condition -- this pier's CPU exposes RAPL counters to a reader with the permissions we have. Nothing in the tree had taken that read.
think I nearly wrote the instrument for it. The ABSENCE habit is what stopped me: tools/fixtures/e/energy_instrument_scan.sh already stood, built for exactly this question, and its header states the distinction I would have had to learn -- existence against readability, since a powercap domain can stand in sysfs at mode 0400 and refuse every read.
obs The read answers no. joule_source=none, powercap_domains=0, hwmon_energy=0, supply_power=0, msr_device=no, tier=counters. No joule is readable on this pier by anybody, so the millijoule witness row 6 named cannot be built here at all -- the assumption failed rather than the falsifier firing, which is a stronger result and a different one.
obs The same scan reads hw_instructions=yes and perf_event_paranoid=2, and paranoid 2 permits a process to count its own user space. perf_event_open(2) reaches that from Rye directly, which matters because this host carries no perf binary. So the unit changes and the SHAPE row 6 asked for -- a counter beside bytes and wall time in a Meter row -- survives whole.
obs The measurement is decisive and I did not expect it to be. Sixteen runs of a fixed million-iteration loop, five times, at a one-minute load average of 10.11: instruction spread 356 to 357 ppm, wall spread 195,724 to 1,422,106 ppm. Three orders of magnitude apart, and the wall figure's own range moves 7.3x where the counter's moves one part per million. The noise is itself noisy.
obs The doubling leg exists because a counter returning a constant would hold a spread of zero and mean nothing -- moonshot 1's own trap, one row over, where an index-only assert proves arithmetic. Doubling the workload gives 1,999,977 ppm, identical to the last digit on every run taken.
obs Aether's sentence governed the control. Both measured gates are mutated in a throwaway pen and required to bite: the spread ceiling dropped to zero reds the spread, a workload ignoring its scale reds the doubling. The unmutated copy is built and run beside them, since a control planting only refusals proves a program that refuses everything just as well as a correct one.
obs A host is not a fault (%646). Where perf_event_open refuses, the program prints counter=unavailable and reaches GREEN, so a machine without a counter keeps this guard green. What IS gated is the distinction -- exactly one branch named, every run.
obs The card had two bytes of headroom at HEAD, 40,958 against 40,960, so my account was rewritten five times to fit inside the elder's own footprint. It lands at 40,959.
obs Both reds were closed by peers before my rebase landed, and both peers did it better. BAKERY moved the same say above the same assert at 20260911.072500; PATCHOULI replaced grep -q with grep -n and said the capture, which reports on the green path as well as the refusing one. I took theirs on the rebase, and their repair carried unsaid_rostered to 935 against a ceiling of 936, so I lowered the ceiling to meet the fall their work earned.
obs That is the card's own open question firing again: nothing in the ledger shows a red is being worked, so three hands spent one morning on two lines. My cold pass read the reds at 07:13 and BAKERY's repair landed at 07:25, which no reading available to me could have shown.
